## 8. Evaluation Metrics

Your manual explains the following metrics for evaluating classification models. Assignment_10

### A. Accuracy

Accuracy measures the percentage of correct predictions.

\[
Accuracy=\frac{TP+TN}{TP+TN+FP+FN}
\]

Using our example:

\[
Accuracy=\frac{20+69}{100}=89\%
\]

### B. Misclassification Rate

It measures the percentage of incorrect predictions.

\[
Misclassification\ Rate=\frac{FP+FN}{Total}
\]

\[
=\frac{5+6}{100}=11\%
\]

Remember:

\[
Misclassification\ Rate=1-Accuracy
\]

### C. Precision

Precision measures how many customers predicted to leave actually left.

\[
Precision=\frac{TP}{TP+FP}
\]

\[
=\frac{20}{20+5}=80\%
\]

### D. Recall

Recall measures how many customers who actually left were correctly identified.

\[
Recall=\frac{TP}{TP+FN}
\]

\[
=\frac{20}{20+6}\approx76.92\%
\]

### E. F1 Score

F1 Score combines precision and recall into one metric.

\[
F1=2\times\frac{Precision\times Recall}{Precision+Recall}
\]

A higher F1 Score indicates a better balance between precision and recall.

### F. ROC Curve

ROC stands for Receiver Operating Characteristic.

It is a graph used to evaluate a classification model at different classification thresholds.

- Y-axis: True Positive Rate.
- X-axis: False Positive Rate.

Your manual explains the ROC curve on page 7. Assignment_10

